VALUES ('0a3d97b7-70b5-4939-875e-6c4a5388ef3d', '00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000400', 'In the mid nineteenth century, many Germans were driven by nationalistic feelings to support a unified Germany. In 1815, the Congress of Vienna created the German Confederation, which consisted of 39 separate autonomous states. While the Austrian Empire usually dominated the German Confederation, the state of Prussia took the lead in unifying them into Germany. The 1848 revolution failed to establish a unified German state.', 'G10-History-STB-2023-web.pdf p.1', '2026.1', 'published', '[-0.016730372,0.032881074,-0.027740465,0.006738864,0.04032266,-0.019176554,-0.011784248,-0.01668846,0.023383547,-0.10724334,-0.043358915,0.020679016,0.039469767,0.01975333,-0.0076383385,-0.04857895,-0.008581892,0.049350414,0.039032135,0.040895954,0.028866054,-0.029588323,0.033902362,-0.020796167,-0.02650433,-0.011456265,-0.036531862,-0.04299268,-0.0131128235,0.19655825,-0.011834919,-0.0066134734,0.018547572,0.001156231,-0.040806815,0.022047775,-0.0011184944,-0.027913766,0.033678245,0.007990508,0.0069730035,0.03023466,-0.03583032,-0.013331848,-0.026249895,-0.006864418,-0.010713369,0.05408389,0.033826448,-0.0024283463,0.015250945,0.02482319,-0.0014968426,-0.042939913,0.03427487,0.0056150076,-0.019008094,0.06202051,0.0016193512,0.00097111304,-0.019641116,0.059334703,0.011447942,-0.004704261,-0.0014990243,0.0072338195,-0.020968582,-0.041125875,0.019335529,-0.023030601,-0.0039604763,-0.0072109876,-0.0068593794,0.00018106731,-0.013171196,-0.0006800894,-0.014012079,0.016324556,0.031337015,0.027212774,0.058071498,0.02055083,0.008648503,0.046187624,-0.016309764,0.00846442,0.0054708663,-0.032311883,0.009936335,-0.0022957665,-0.008999323,-0.011088475,0.035683513,-0.028457465,0.025850307,-0.02194822,-0.047295783,0.00032660482,0.029990949,-0.035594888,0.030518528,0.015222998,-0.008182534,0.05725872,0.023619622,0.007884888,-0.04376369,-0.01718576,0.0046965866,0.03075603,-0.0189623,-0.292668,-0.03076028,-0.018267