VALUES ('d6aa99b8-42f8-4808-b5d9-a42cc5bf6868', '00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000400', 'Russia, Great Britain, France, Austria-Hungary, Italy and Germany followed their own national interests in the Balkan region. The foreign powers intervened for their own ends in the struggles between the Turks and the nationalist groups. Russia: Russia supported the Balkan nationalists for several reasons: The Russians were Slavs, like the Bulgarians and the Serbs. They were Orthodox Christians as were many of the discontented Balkan groups. Moreover, Russia wanted to gain access to the Black Sea and the Mediterranean Sea. Britain: Britain’s main concern was to protect its interests in India and did not want the Russians in the Mediterranean, where they might challenge their sea power. They supported the Turks to suppress the nationalist movements.', 'G10-History-STB-2023-web.pdf p.1', '2026.1', 'published', '[0.003394723,0.007977942,0.0024574825,0.005132153,0.031116247,-0.027162611,-0.0089203315,0.005580187,0.0015201524,-0.09981072,-0.027661996,0.009113875,0.052672844,-0.006927289,-0.0642626,-0.0021131583,-0.012297167,0.008643346,0.04310385,0.00233456,0.03468272,-0.019861529,0.028716618,0.010668544,-0.0055062757,0.0060726767,0.010796543,-0.06237355,-0.0024675084,0.17820701,-0.010203398,0.014293691,-0.00023027684,0.018559406,-0.020168627,-0.000021971577,0.020068849,-0.05066992,-0.023613825,-0.011384192,-0.006118505,-0.011088744,0.05064752,0.007916219,0.03542029,-0.0019006049,0.0030352902,0.049903013,-0.010069614,0.030420247,-0.008282532,0.03889147,-0.002426867,-0.09146709,0.0392636,0.042267136,0.018336093,0.0014916303,0.01984672,0.007683759,0.028143248,0.0076525835,0.0006216066,0.024013132,0.0074489806,-0.01732114,0.00043703447,-0.06171929,0.023885641,0.027452769,0.04289273,0.013967057,0.023797993,0.03374222,0.0037957027,0.010042288,-0.075351015,0.029678285,0.07440893,0.007027566,0.023423169,0.013404871,0.031427324,0.022819402,0.00685537,0.03833881,0.0071256594,-0.03348525,0.011