VALUES ('ef7540a1-ccc9-4162-ac4b-5b14e6bc127e', '00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000400', 'Read the following poem entitled “The White Man’s Burden” written by Rudyard Kipling and answer the question below: 1. How does Kipling describe the subjects of colonial rule? History Grade 10 Student Textbook Take up the White Man’s Burden Send forth the best ye breed Go bind your sons to exile To serve your captive’s need; To wait in heavy harness, On fluttered folk and wild Your new-caught, sullen peoples, Half-devil and half child. (source: http://historymatters.mu. edu/d/5478/ )', 'G10-History-STB-2023-web.pdf p.1', '2026.1', 'published', '[0.0060597355,0.020544903,0.018295614,-0.006075043,0.012297908,-0.028633,-0.021809973,-0.01504156,-0.009867695,-0.092953496,0.00495504,0.04347267,0.042986263,-0.0012389261,-0.038402673,-0.020985689,0.015326436,-0.00015919327,0.017203555,0.021147143,0.027887069,-0.017881388,0.0032690384,0.023294587,-0.008992368,-0.010120967,-0.013731491,-0.021061841,-0.0019855048,0.17898607,-0.011937378,-0.009497438,0.002990673,0.010278375,0.0082865255,0.044314936,0.0040639527,-0.04965698,0.033938546,-0.025134103,-0.0026193857,-0.0030690155,-0.0077997483,0.047230504,0.011176376,-0.0080327615,-0.032686774,0.012907857,-0.007961656,0.011119849,-0.05660749,0.00052779797,-0.00572494,-0.04804728,-0.0020118882,0.019170184,-0.038145542,0.016157659,-0.026474742,0.046000913,-0.02375509,-0.002539,0.012993027,0.009751581,0.007398575,-0.027653133,-0.0056878426,-0.04666142,0.058415536,-0.02339057,0.000927366,-0.010095305,-0.0014777131,-0.014748441,-0.023553925,-0.005422527,-0.07509774,-0.012714865,0.021562325,0.0272775,0.031756975,0.021629376,-0.024642246,0.018307399,0.0060178316,-0.03683266,-0.04352278,0.0035819921,0.010207617,0.039581858,0.011829769,-0.0016714258,0.0018272037,-0.055347454,0.0058354745,-0.005131764,0.013945074,-0.02902835,-0.007270552,-0.015834415,-0.052938383,0.014722942,0.032975066,-0.012149085,0.021043349,0.010022987,-0.0041388525,-0.0052065267,0.01