VALUES ('ec3f7f22-9585-4228-b303-f6196d681e04', '00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000400', 'In 1897, Kafa was incorporated after the forces of Tato Gaki Sherocho (the last king of Kafa) were defeated by Menilek’s army led by Ras Wolde Giorgis. Similarly, Emperor Menilek extended his authority over Benishangul and Gambella, setting the stage for a formal agreement in I902 on borders with the British as the colonial power in Sudan. The process of territorial expansion was concluded with the signing of boundary agreements with the neighboring colonial powers that continued until 1908.', 'G10-History-STB-2023-web.pdf p.1', '2026.1', 'published', '[0.044928957,-0.0050757374,0.014329253,-0.019076556,0.031226166,-0.013928378,-0.0027187474,-0.055860803,-0.016472768,-0.13118881,-0.024785778,-0.021680104,0.035960495,0.032750618,-0.055683352,-0.030765504,-0.010923109,0.009554228,0.027717713,-0.027202377,0.04021672,-0.0045516826,0.019659884,0.01970458,-0.041110404,-0.000678962,0.00485376,-0.07488347,-0.01769962,0.18958387,-0.011313099,-0.021132477,-0.011242277,-0.02052108,-0.009773228,-0.008474775,-0.00815482,0.029206337,0.028071215,-0.03770837,0.026192175,-0.00092701096,-0.027964976,0.018666284,0.02528738,-0.055874463,0.010544836,0.01774485,-0.023095282,0.009403748,0.016407557,0.001705329,0.020635989,-0.053983897,0.017929714,-0.0043844082,0.045588586,0.006747683,0.039983477,0.02853676,0.0002147994,-0.009258778,-0.028561808,0.014627086,-0.05146638,0.050740156,0.030133525,-0.0021762482,0.039724696,0.030731406,0.03797315,-0.0051133167,0.00031989478,0.027261449,-0.029338475,0.023635287,-0.04387784,-0.0034509175,0.078572944,0.0127575835,0.05645602,0.050374933,-0.036652267,0.034449507,-0.041259345,-0.012529621,-0.015588261,-0.015092181,0.010412183,0.0026016908,-0.038526107,0.0023135864,-0.007700253,-0.0586047,0.04083343,0.024546737,-0.015526987,0.00337228,0.007842748,0.0051363693,0.0002593051,0.009857655,0.018955594,0.013978973,0.023638025,0.021052688,-0.020042894,-0.009425405,0.051912